#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065104} :activity/id #uuid "8d3261ec-ded8-5b6d-ac21-5c0ada0ad6a0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049597 :topic/id #uuid "03616d92-38bb-52d1-b636-cc62f67b859d" :topic/math-academy-id 350} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065104 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065437 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find all of the values of $x$ that satisfy *both* $3x+9 \\geq 0$ *and* $2x \\leq -2$ simultaneously. \n\nTo do this, we solve each inequality individually and then compute the intersection of the two solutions.\n\n- We start by solving $3x + 9 \\geq 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+9 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 3x+9-9 & \\ge 0-9 \\\\ 3x & \\ge -9 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & \\ge \\frac{-9}{3} \\\\ x & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this inequality is shown on the number line below.\n\n![](images/51/5127629c09f32bb8ed7872b476322d6973e44e82be7977492c8dd0967d3cb0ec.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x \\leq -2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\le -2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ x & \\le -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this inequality is shown on the number line below.\n\n![](images/35/35e30bc9c45b08793d847c8750698f7d9dab781438405239ed4483ce82f2dcfb.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/fe/fe4c223767cb06d9d620d32f5e668c7305688b3870bf0317304c56b11053e19f.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $\\color{blue}-3 \\leq x \\leq -1.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "79460753-2a4c-5227-8dcd-7355a1841558" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8687 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f583864f-f671-5e7b-bc34-8fcce050be85" :step/math-academy-id 171168 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065105}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065105 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064237 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063973 :question/id #uuid "f55392b5-8cb5-516c-8151-051